{{also|House}} ==English==
===Etymology 1=== {{etymon|en|id=building|:inh|enm:hous<id:house>|tree=1}} {{wikidata lexeme|L512}} {{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)kewH-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|hous}}, {{m|enm|hus}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hūs|t=dwelling, shelter, house}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hūs}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hūsą|t=house}}, possibly from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)kews-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kewH-|t=to cover, hide}}. More at {{l|en|hose}}.
Eclipsed non-native {{noncog|enm|mees}}, {{m|enm|meson}}, {{m|enm|measoun|t=house}}, borrowed from {{noncog|xno|mes}}, {{m|fro|mies}}, {{m|fro|meis}}, {{m|fro|maisun|t=house}}. The uncommon plural form ''housen'' is from {{inh|en|enm|husen}}, {{m|enm|housen}}. (The Old English nominative plural was simply {{m|ang|hūs}}.) {{col-top|2|cog}} Cognate with {{cog|sco|hoose}}, {{m|sco|oos|t=house}}, {{cog|yol|heouse}}, {{m|yol|houze}}, {{m|yol|howze|t=house}}, {{cog|frr|hüs|t=house}}, {{cog|stq|Huus}}, {{m|stq|Húus|t=house}}, {{cog|fy|hûs|t=house}}, {{cog|gsw|hous}}, {{m|gsw|hus}}, {{m|gsw|husch}}, {{m|gsw|hüs}}, {{m|gsw|hüüsch|t=house}}, {{cog|bar|-}}, {{cog|cim|-}}, {{cog|mhn|haus|t=house}}, {{cog|gmw-cfr|Haus}}, {{m|gmw-cfr|Hous}}, {{m|gmw-cfr|Huus|t=home}}, {{cog|nl|huis|t=house}}, {{cog|nds-nl|hoes}}, {{m|nds-nl|huus|t=house}}, {{cog|de|Haus}}, {{m|de|Hauß|t=house}}, {{cog|nds-de|Huus|t=house}}, {{cog|li|hoes}}, {{m|li|Huus|t=house}}, {{cog|lb|Haus|t=house}}, {{cog|wym|haojs}}, {{m|wym|haus}}, {{m|wym|hoüz|t=house}}, {{cog|yi|הויז|t=house}}, {{cog|da,nb,nn,sv|hus|t=house}}, {{cog|ovd|aus|t=house}}, {{cog|fo,is|hús|t=house}}, {{cog|gme-cgo|hus|t=house}}; also {{cog|kw|kudha|t=to conceal, hide}}, {{cog|cy|cuddio|t=to hide}}, {{cog|la|cutis|t=human skin; hide, leather}}, {{cog|grc|κεύθω|t=to cover, hide}}, {{cog|xto|kāc|t=hide, skin}}, {{cog|sa|स्कुनाति|t=to cover}}. {{col-bottom}}
