|passage=Towards the following morning, the thermometer fell to 5°; and at daylight, there was not an atom of '''water''' to be seen in any direction.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Arthur T. Hubbard|title=Encyclopedia of Surface and Colloid Science|isbn=0824707966|page=4895
|passage=A '''water''' drop placed on the surface of ice can either spread or form a lens depending on the properties of the three phases involved in wetting, i.e., on the properties of the ice, '''water''', and gas phases.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-05-11|volume=407|issue=8835|page=80|magazine=w:The Economist| url=http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21577341-worlds-third-largest-area-ice-about-undergo-systematic|title=The climate of Tibet: Pole-land| passage=Of all the transitions brought about on the Earth’s surface by temperature change, the melting of ice into '''water''' is the starkest. It is binary. And for the land beneath, the air above and the life around, it changes everything.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/RCa6m|archivedate=2023-03-10}}
