#* {{RQ:King James Version|Luke|19|26|passage=... unto every one that '''hath''' shall be given, and from him that '''hath''' not, even that he '''hath''' shall be taken away ...}}
#* {{RQ:Swift Gulliver|part=III|page=108|passage=I could plainly diſcover from whence one Family derives a long Chin; why a ſecond '''hath''' abounded with Knaves for two Generations, and Fools for two more; why a third happened to be crack-brained, and a fourth to be Sharpers.}}
#* {{RQ:Fielding Tom Jones|volume=IV|chapter=I|passage=To be plain, I much question whether the politician, who '''hath''' generally a good nose, '''hath''' not scented out somewhat of the utility of this practice.}}

