====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|say||th-form}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Exodus|8|1|text=And the {{smallcaps|Lord}} spake unto Moses, Go unto Pharaoh, and say unto him, Thus '''saith''' the LORD, Let my people go, that they may serve me.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Malachi|3|17|passage=And they shall be mine, [[saith]] the {{smallcaps|Lord}} of hosts, in that day when I make up my jewels; and I will spare them, as a man [[spareth]] his own son that [[serveth]] him.}}
#* {{RQ:Burton Melancholy|edition=2nd}}, B. Blake (1836), p.663
#*: In this life we have but a glimpse of this beauty and happiness; we shall hereafter, as John '''saith''', see him as he is.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1850|author=w:Dante Gabriel Rossetti|title=w:The Blessed Damozel|section=ll. 89-90
|passage=While every leaf that His plumes touch / '''Saith''' His Name audibly.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1855|author=w:Robert Browning|title=s:Childe Roland to the Dark Tower Came|section=V
|passage={{...}} ("since all is o'er," he '''saith''', / "And the blow fallen no grieving can amend;")}}
#* {{quote-av|en|author=w:Sean Hannity; w:Sean Penn|title=Sean Penn joins Sean Hannity to discuss Russian invasion of Ukraine|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220411055322/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IfUORitTEBI|archivedate=11 April 2022|series=w:Hannity|publisher=w:Fox News|date=April 5, 2022|time=22:33|text=Penn: I don't want to invest in the conversation, not that I don't have it privately, about my feelings about what direct action should happen to a leader who does that, but if there is a God, there will be vengeance beyond all possible comprehension.<br>Hannity: "Vengeance is mine '''saith''' the Lord", quoted in a very famous book.}}

