===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵews-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|chesen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ċēosan|t=to choose, seek out, select, elect, decide, test, accept, settle for, approve}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*keusan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*keusaną|t=to test; to choose}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*ǵéwseti|t=to choose, taste}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*ǵews-|t=to taste, try}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|stq|kjoze|t=to choose}}, {{cog|fy|kieze|t=to choose}}, {{cog|nl|kiezen|t=to choose}}, {{cog|nds|kesen|t=to choose}}, {{cog|de|kiesen|t=to choose}}, {{cog|da|kyse|t=to frighten}}, {{cog|fo,is|kjósa|t=to vote; to elect; to choose; to prefer}}, {{cog|nn|kjosa}}, {{m|nn|kjose|t=to choose}}, {{cog|sv|tjusa|t=to charm; to bewitch}}, {{cog|got|𐌺𐌹𐌿𐍃𐌰𐌽|t=to test}}, {{cog|fr|choisir|t=to choose}}; also {{cog|br|diuz|t=to choose}}, {{cog|kw,cy|dewis|t=to choose}}, {{cog|la|gustō|t=to taste, sample}}, {{cog|grc|γεύω|t=to feed; to taste; to eat; to try; to enjoy}}, {{cog|cs|zkoušet|t=to taste; to examine; to rehearse}}, {{cog|pl|kuszać|t=to eat}}, {{cog|ru|кушать|t=to have a meal, to eat}}, {{cog|sh|ку̏шати}}, {{m|sh|kȕšati|t=to taste; to test}}, {{cog|uk|ку́шати|t=to taste; to eat}}, {{m|uk|куштува́ти|t=to taste}}, {{cog|ae|𐬰𐬀𐬊𐬱𐬀|t=pleasure}}, {{cog|bal,ps|دوست|tr=dost|t=friend}}, {{cog|kmr,zza|dost|t=friend}}, {{cog|fa|دوسْت|tr=dōst / dust|t=friend; boyfriend or girlfriend; loved}}, {{cog|sa|जुषते|t=to enjoy}}.
{{col-bottom}}

