====Verb====
{{en-verb|~s|choosing|chose,~d<l:nonstandard>|chosen,~d<l:nonstandard>,chose<l:now,colloquial>}}

# To [[pick]]; to make the choice of; to select.
#: {{ux|en|I '''chose''' a nice ripe apple from the fruit bowl.}}
#* {{RQ:Hume Human Nature|book=II|section=Of the Influencing Motives of the Will|page=249|passage=Secondly, VVhen in exerting any paſſion in action, vve '''chuſe''' means inſufficient for the deſign'd end, and deceive ourſelves in our judgment of cauſes and effects.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Christmas Carol|pages=67–68|pageref=68|passage=You may—the memory of what is past half makes me hope you will—have pain in this. A very, very brief time, and you will dismiss the recollection of it, gladly, as an unprofitable dream, from which it happened well that you awoke. May you be happy in the life you have '''chosen'''!}}
#* {{RQ:Rinehart Hopwood Bat|chapter=I|passage=The Bat—they called him the Bat. Like a bat he '''chose''' the night hours for his work of rapine; like a bat he struck and vanished, pouncingly, noiselessly; like a bat he never showed himself to the face of the day.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1997-11-26|work=Ellensburg Daily Record|volume=96|issue=280|location=Ellensburg, Washington|title=Slain teen '''chose''' bad friends|page=9|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=ydQeAAAAIBAJ&pg=PA17&dq=Reena+Virk&article_id=6624,5469066&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiiq47d37yWAxVKJEQIHcSKAXEQ6AF6BAgMEAM#v=onepage&q=Reena%20Virk&f=false|nocolon=1}}
# To [[elect]].
#: {{ux|en|He was '''chosen''' as president in 1990.}}
# To [[decide]] to act in a certain way.
#: {{ux|en|I '''chose''' to walk to work today.}}
# To [[prefer]]; to [[wish]]; to [[desire]].
#* {{RQ:Goldsmith Vicar|passage=The landlady now returned to know if we did not '''choose''' a more genteel apartment.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=Justin Deschamps|passage='''Choose''' truth, and find beauty. '''Choose''' love, and embrace change.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* This is a [[catenative]] verb that takes the ''to infinitive''. See [[Appendix:English catenative verbs]]

